Package: bodybuildr
Type: Package
Title: Build Infographic PDF Pages from Self-Sizing Blocks
Version: 0.5.1
Authors@R: c(
    person(
      "Rafael", "Leon",
      email = "rafa.leon190@gmail.com",
      role = c("aut", "cre")
    ),
    person(
      "Dan", "Alvarez",
      email = "d.alvrzx@gmail.com",
      role = c("aut")
    ))
Maintainer: Rafael Leon <rafa.leon190@gmail.com>
Description: Build infographic-style PDF pages in R from blocks that know
    their own height. Stack and split blocks into columns, mix text, tables,
    ggplot2 plots, images, legends and status marks, and place them between a
    page header and a footer pinned to the bottom margin. Export one or many
    pages to a single PDF with predictable sizing.
SystemRequirements: Cairo (optional but recommended for full UTF-8 PDF output;
    macOS users should install XQuartz from https://www.xquartz.org)
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
LazyData: true
URL: https://bodybuildr.sunstonebio.info/, https://github.com/sunstone-bioinformatics/bodybuildr
BugReports: https://github.com/sunstone-bioinformatics/bodybuildr/issues
RoxygenNote: 7.3.3
